{
  "dom_id": "step-53474",
  "name": "Example: \n                    Dividing With Negative Whole Numbers and Fractions",
  "problem": "Find the value of $\\dfrac{4}{7} \\div (-2).$",
  "worked_solution": "Dividing a positive number by a negative number gives a negative number. Hence, the result will be negative.\n\nTherefore, since \n\n$$\n\\dfrac{4}{7} \\div 2 = \\dfrac{4}{7 \\times 2} = \\dfrac{4}{14} = \\dfrac{2}{7},\n$$\n\nwe obtain\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{4}{7} \\div (-2) = -\\dfrac {2}{7}.\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
